We are identical twins.  This was confirmed with genetic testing.  We also 
have been shown to be identical mirror twins.  All mirror twins must also 
be identical.  I also detected some relatively rare genes in myself while 
taking genetics experimentation courses, and personally detected these 
genes in my brother.

Nonidentical twins occur when two eggs are fertilized with two eggs.  These 
form two blastulae which develop independently into two different fetuses.

Identical (nonmirror) twins occur when a single egg is fertilized with a 
single sperm.  The early cell(s) split into two distinct blastulae in the 
womb, with each developing into a distinct fetus.  This split occurs before 
the cells start differentiating into specific kinds of cells.

Identical mirror twins occur when the blastula starts to differentiate into 
specific different kinds of cells and *then* decides to split.  Enough 
differentiation has occured to determine which end will be the head, which 
is the foot, and which is right and left.  Because of this, mirror twins 
are mirror copies of one another.  One of the twins will be right-handed, 
while the other is left.  One of the twins will have all internal organs 
reversed, and one will have the usual configuration.

I am the right-handed twin, with all the default internal configuration.
My brother is left-handed, with all his organs reversed.
